{"task_id": "HumanEval/1", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\ndef separate_paren_groups(paren_string: str) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Separates balanced, non-nested parenthesis groups from an input string, ignoring spaces.\n    Returns a list of these separate group strings.\n    >>> separate_paren_groups('( ) (( )) (( )( ))')\n    ['()', '(())', '(()())']\n    \"\"\"\n    # Ignore any spaces in the input string.\n    cleaned_string = paren_string.replace(' ', '')\n\n    result: List[str] = []\n    balance: int = 0\n    current_group_start: int = 0\n\n    # Identify separate, balanced, non-nested groups.\n    for i in range(len(cleaned_string)):\n        char = cleaned_string[i]\n        if char == '(':\n            balance += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            balance -= 1\n\n        # A top-level balanced group ends when balance returns to 0.\n        if balance == 0:\n            # Extract the group and add to result.\n            group = cleaned_string[current_group_start : i + 1]\n            result.append(group)\n            # Set the start for the next potential group.\n            current_group_start = i + 1\n\n    # Return a list of strings.\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/0", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef has_close_elements(numbers: List[float], threshold: float) -> bool:\n    \"\"\" Check if in given list of numbers, are any two numbers closer to each other than\n    given threshold.\n    >>> has_close_elements([1.0, 2.0, 3.0], 0.5)\n    False\n    >>> has_close_elements([1.0, 2.8, 3.0, 4.0, 5.0, 2.0], 0.3)\n    True\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n    # Iterate through all unique pairs of numbers in the list.\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            # Calculate the absolute difference and check if it's strictly less than the threshold.\n            if abs(numbers[i] - numbers[j]) < threshold:\n                return True\n    return False"}
