{"task_id": "HumanEval/21", "solution": "from typing import List\n\n\ndef rescale_to_unit(numbers: List[float]) -> List[float]:\n    \"\"\"Given a list of numbers, linearly transforms them so the smallest becomes 0.0 and the largest becomes 1.0.\n    All other numbers are scaled proportionally within this [0.0, 1.0] interval.\n    \"\"\"\n    min_value = min(numbers)\n    max_value = max(numbers)\n\n    scaled_numbers: List[float] = []\n\n    if min_value == max_value:\n        # If all numbers are the same, map all to 0.0 as per design specification.\n        for _ in numbers:\n            scaled_numbers.append(0.0)\n    else:\n        # Apply the linear transformation.\n        for number in numbers:\n            scaled_value = (number - min_value) / (max_value - min_value)\n            scaled_numbers.append(scaled_value)\n\n    return scaled_numbers"}
