{"task_id": "HumanEval/26", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\nclass IntegerList:\n    \"\"\"Manages an integer list to identify and remove duplicate elements.\"\"\"\n    _input_elements: List[int]\n    _output_elements: List[int]\n\n    def __init__(self, numbers: List[int]):\n        \"\"\"Initializes the IntegerList with the provided input numbers.\"\"\"\n        self._input_elements = numbers\n        self._output_elements = []\n\n    def process_duplicates(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Identifies and stores unique elements from the input list, preserving order.\"\"\"\n        counts = {}\n        # First pass to count occurrences of each number\n        for num in self._input_elements:\n            counts[num] = counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n        # Second pass to build the output list with only unique elements\n        for num in self._input_elements:\n            if counts[num] == 1:\n                self._output_elements.append(num)\n\n    def get_output(self) -> List[int]:\n        \"\"\"Returns the list of unique integers in their original relative order.\"\"\"\n        return self._output_elements\n\n\ndef remove_duplicates(numbers: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    From a list of integers, remove all elements that occur more than once.\n    Keep order of elements left the same as in the input.\n    \"\"\"\n    list_processor = IntegerList(numbers)\n    list_processor.process_duplicates()\n    return list_processor.get_output()\n```"}
