{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Exception raised for invalid input to the Polynomial Zero Finder.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef poly(xs: list[float], x: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates polynomial with coefficients xs at point x.\n    Returns xs[0] + xs[1]*x + xs[2]*x^2 + ... + xs[n]*x^n.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum([coeff * math.pow(x, i) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs)])\n\nclass Polynomial:\n    \"\"\"\n    Represents a polynomial, handles validation and zero-point calculation.\n    Coefficients are stored from constant term to highest degree.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, coefficients: list[float]):\n        self.coefficients = coefficients\n        self._validate_even_coefficients()\n        self._validate_largest_non_zero_coefficient()\n\n    def _validate_even_coefficients(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates that the coefficient list has an even number of elements.\"\"\"\n        if len(self.coefficients) % 2 != 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input list must have an even number of coefficients.\")\n\n    def _validate_largest_non_zero_coefficient(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates that the highest degree coefficient is non-zero.\"\"\"\n        if not self.coefficients or self.coefficients[-1] == 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Largest non-zero coefficient must be present.\")\n\n    def calculate_zero_point(self) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Finds a single zero point of the polynomial using the bisection method.\n        It assumes an odd-degree polynomial, guaranteeing at least one real root.\n        \"\"\"\n        low, high = -100.0, 100.0\n        f_low = poly(self.coefficients, low)\n        f_high = poly(self.coefficients, high)\n\n        while f_low * f_high > 0:\n            low *= 2\n            high *= 2\n            f_low = poly(self.coefficients, low)\n            f_high = poly(self.coefficients, high)\n\n        tolerance = 1e-6\n        max_iterations = 100\n\n        for _ in range(max_iterations):\n            mid = (low + high) / 2\n            f_mid = poly(self.coefficients, mid)\n\n            if abs(f_mid) < tolerance:\n                return mid\n\n            if f_low * f_mid < 0:\n                high = mid\n                # f_high effectively becomes f_mid for the next iteration\n            else:\n                low = mid\n                f_low = f_mid\n\n        return (low + high) / 2\n\ndef find_zero(xs: list[float]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates a single zero point for a polynomial given its coefficients.\n    It orchestrates polynomial creation, input validation, and root finding.\n    \"\"\"\n    polynomial = Polynomial(xs)\n    return polynomial.calculate_zero_point()\n```"}
