{"task_id": "HumanEval/32", "solution": "import math\n\n\ndef poly(xs: list, x: float):\n    \"\"\"\n    Evaluates polynomial with coefficients xs at point x.\n    return xs[0] + xs[1] * x + xs[1] * x^2 + .... xs[n] * x^n\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum([coeff * math.pow(x, i) for i, coeff in enumerate(xs)])\n\n\ndef find_zero(xs: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    xs are coefficients of a polynomial. find_zero finds x such that poly(x) = 0.\\n    It returns a single zero point using an iterative search method.\\n    \"\"\"\n    # CRITICAL: Validation checks for FR5 and FR6, and associated ValueError exceptions,\n    # are omitted as per explicit \"CRITICAL REQUIREMENTS\" not to raise exceptions for edge cases.\n    # The implementation trusts the caller's inputs and assumes conditions for a solution are met.\n\n    tolerance = 1e-6\n    max_iterations = 1000\n\n    # Step 1: Find an interval [a, b] where poly(a) and poly(b) have opposite signs.\n    # Start with a small interval around zero and expand until a bracket is found.\n    a, b = -1.0, 1.0\n    fa, fb = poly(xs, a), poly(xs, b)\n\n    while fa * fb > 0 and abs(b) < 1e9: # Expand search range, limit to avoid extreme values\n        if abs(fa) < tolerance: return a\n        if abs(fb) < tolerance: return b\n        a *= 2.0\n        b *= 2.0\n        fa, fb = poly(xs, a), poly(xs, b)\n\n    # Step 2: Perform bisection method on the bracketed interval [a, b].\n    for _ in range(max_iterations):\n        mid = (a + b) / 2.0\n        f_mid = poly(xs, mid)\n\n        if abs(f_mid) < tolerance:\n            return mid\n\n        # Determine which half of the interval contains the root\n        if poly(xs, a) * f_mid < 0:\n            b = mid\n        else:\n            a = mid\n\n    # Return the midpoint of the final interval as the best approximation\n    return (a + b) / 2.0"}
