{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_third(l: list):\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a list l' such that\n    l' is identical to l in the indicies that are not divisible by three, while its values at the indicies that are divisible by three are equal\n    to the values of the corresponding indicies of l, but sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    l_prime = list(l)  # Create a shallow copy of the input list.\n    temporary_divisible_elements = []\n    temporary_divisible_indices = []\n\n    # Identify and collect elements and their indices at positions divisible by three.\n    for i in range(len(l)):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            temporary_divisible_elements.append(l[i])\n            temporary_divisible_indices.append(i)\n\n    temporary_divisible_elements.sort()  # Sort the collected elements in ascending order.\n\n    # Place the sorted elements back into l' at their original divisible-by-three positions.\n    for k in range(len(temporary_divisible_indices)):\n        original_divisible_index = temporary_divisible_indices[k]\n        l_prime[original_divisible_index] = temporary_divisible_elements[k]\n\n    return l_prime\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/33", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_third(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"This function takes a list l and returns a new list l' where elements at indices\n    divisible by three are sorted, and other elements maintain their original positions.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(l)\n    l_prime = [None] * n\n\n    divisible_elements = []\n    divisible_indices = []\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        if i % 3 == 0:\n            divisible_elements.append(l[i])\n            divisible_indices.append(i)\n        else:\n            l_prime[i] = l[i]\n\n    divisible_elements.sort()\n\n    sorted_idx_counter = 0\n    for original_divisible_idx in divisible_indices:\n        l_prime[original_divisible_idx] = divisible_elements[sorted_idx_counter]\n        sorted_idx_counter += 1\n\n    return l_prime\n```"}
