{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence iteratively.\n    This implementation avoids recursion and uses O(1) space complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize the last four fib4 numbers: fib4(i-4), fib4(i-3), fib4(i-2), fib4(i-1)\n    a, b, c, d = 0, 0, 2, 0  # Represents fib4(0), fib4(1), fib4(2), fib4(3)\n\n    for _ in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = a + b + c + d\n        a = b\n        b = c\n        c = d\n        d = next_fib\n\n    return d\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/46", "solution": "```python\ndef fib4(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the Fib4 number sequence iteratively. The sequence is defined by base cases for n=0, 1, 2, 3 and fib4(n) = fib4(n-1) + fib4(n-2) + fib4(n-3) + fib4(n-4) for n > 3.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 0\n\n    fib_sequence = [0, 0, 2, 0]\n\n    for i in range(4, n + 1):\n        next_fib = fib_sequence[i-1] + fib_sequence[i-2] + fib_sequence[i-3] + fib_sequence[i-4]\n        fib_sequence.append(next_fib)\n\n    return fib_sequence[n]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    Handles both odd and even sized lists, returning int or float as appropriate.\n    \"\"\"\n    sorted_l = sorted(l)\n    n = len(sorted_l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # For an odd number of elements, the median is the middle element.\n        median_value = sorted_l[n // 2]\n    else:\n        # For an even number of elements, the median is the average of the two middle elements.\n        mid1 = sorted_l[n // 2 - 1]\n        mid2 = sorted_l[n // 2]\n        median_value = (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n\n    # Convert to int if the median has no fractional part, otherwise return as float.\n    if median_value == int(median_value):\n        return int(median_value)\n    else:\n        return float(median_value)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/47", "solution": "```python\ndef median(l: list):\n    \"\"\"Return median of elements in the list l.\n    >>> median([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    3\n    >>> median([-10, 4, 6, 1000, 10, 20])\n    15.0\n    \"\"\"\n    l.sort()\n    n = len(l)\n\n    if n % 2 == 1:\n        # Odd length list, return the middle element\n        return float(l[n // 2])\n    else:\n        # Even length list, return the average of the two middle elements\n        mid1 = l[(n // 2) - 1]\n        mid2 = l[n // 2]\n        return (mid1 + mid2) / 2.0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/48", "solution": "```python\ndef is_palindrome(text: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if given string is a palindrome based on specific rules.\n    Empty strings are palindromes; non-alphanumeric characters are ignored, and comparison is case-insensitive.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return True\n\n    processed_chars = [char.lower() for char in text if char.isalnum()]\n    processed_text = \"\".join(processed_chars)\n\n    reversed_text = processed_text[::-1]\n\n    return processed_text == reversed_text\n```"}
