{"task_id": "HumanEval/59", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_prime_factor(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the largest prime factor of n.\n    This function assumes n > 1 and n is not a prime number.\n    \"\"\"\n    largest_factor = 1\n\n    # Handle factor 2\n    while n % 2 == 0:\n        largest_factor = 2\n        n //= 2\n\n    # Check for odd factors from 3 up to sqrt(n)\n    d = 3\n    while d * d <= n:\n        while n % d == 0:\n            largest_factor = d\n            n //= d\n        d += 2\n\n    # If n is still greater than 1, it must be the largest prime factor\n    if n > 1:\n        largest_factor = n\n\n    return largest_factor\n```"}
