{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "```python\n_fibfib_cache = {}\n\ndef fibfib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"The FibFib number sequence is defined by specific base cases and a recursive formula.\n    This function efficiently computes the n-th element using memoization.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _fibfib_cache:\n        return _fibfib_cache[n]\n\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        result = 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        result = 1\n    else:\n        result = fibfib(n - 1) + fibfib(n - 2) + fibfib(n - 3)\n\n    _fibfib_cache[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "def _get_digit_count(s):\n    \"\"\"Returns the number of digits in the string representation of an integer.\"\"\"\n    return len(s)\n\ndef _perform_circular_right_shift(s, amount):\n    \"\"\"Performs a circular right shift on string 's' by 'amount' positions.\"\"\"\n    return s[-amount:] + s[:-amount]\n\ndef _reverse_string(s):\n    \"\"\"Reverses the order of characters in the given string.\"\"\"\n    return s[::-1]\n\ndef circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Circular shift the digits of the integer x, shift the digits right by shift\n    and return the result as a string.\n    If shift > number of digits, return digits reversed.\n    >>> circular_shift(12, 1)\n    \"21\"\n    >>> circular_shift(12, 2)\n    \"12\"\n    \"\"\"\n    s_x = str(x)\n    digit_count = _get_digit_count(s_x)\n\n    if shift > digit_count:\n        return _reverse_string(s_x)\n    else:\n        return _perform_circular_right_shift(s_x, shift)"}
