{"task_id": "HumanEval/84", "solution": "```python\ndef _validate_input(N: int) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Validates if N is within the allowed range [0, 10000].\n    Raises ValueError if N is outside this range.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (0 <= N <= 10000):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input N must be between 0 and 10000, inclusive.\")\n\ndef _calculate_sum_of_digits(N: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the decimal digits of N.\n    Converts N to a string to iterate through its digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    sum_val = 0\n    for digit_char in str(N):\n        sum_val += int(digit_char)\n    return sum_val\n\ndef _convert_to_binary_string(sum_val: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Converts an integer sum_val into its binary string representation.\n    Uses Python's bin() function and handles the special case for 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if sum_val == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n    return bin(sum_val)[2:]\n\ndef solve(N: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Given a positive integer N, return the total sum of its digits in binary.\n\n    Example\n        For N = 1000, the sum of digits will be 1 the output should be \"1\".\n        For N = 150, the sum of digits will be 6 the output should be \"110\".\n        For N = 147, the sum of digits will be 12 the output should be \"1100\".\n\n    Variables:\n        @N integer\n             Constraints: 0 \u2264 N \u2264 10000.\n    Output:\n         a string of binary number\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(N)\n    sum_of_digits = _calculate_sum_of_digits(N)\n    return _convert_to_binary_string(sum_of_digits)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/83", "solution": "```python\ndef starts_one_ends(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the count of n-digit positive integers that start with 1 or end with 1.\n    This count is derived using the inclusion-exclusion principle.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        # The only 1-digit number is 1, which starts and ends with 1.\n        return 1\n    elif n == 2:\n        # N-digit numbers starting with 1: 10-19 (10 numbers)\n        # N-digit numbers ending with 1: 11, 21, ..., 91 (9 numbers)\n        # N-digit numbers starting AND ending with 1: 11 (1 number)\n        # Total = 10 + 9 - 1 = 18\n        return 18\n    else: # n > 2\n        # Count of n-digit numbers starting with 1: 10**(n-1)\n        # Count of n-digit numbers ending with 1: 9 * 10**(n-2) (first digit cannot be 0)\n        # Count of n-digit numbers starting AND ending with 1: 10**(n-2)\n        # Total = 10**(n-1) + 9 * 10**(n-2) - 10**(n-2)\n        #       = 10**(n-1) + 8 * 10**(n-2)\n        #       = 10 * 10**(n-2) + 8 * 10**(n-2)\n        #       = 18 * 10**(n-2)\n        return 18 * (10**(n - 2))\n\n```"}
