{"task_id": "HumanEval/115", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\n# --- Data Models (as per models.py) ---\nclass WaterUnit:\n    \"\"\"Represents a single unit of water.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: int):\n        self.value = value\n\nclass Well:\n    \"\"\"Represents a single well containing water units.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, water_units_data: list[int]):\n        self.water_units = [WaterUnit(unit) for unit in water_units_data]\n        self.total_water_in_well = sum(unit.value for unit in self.water_units)\n\nclass Grid:\n    \"\"\"Represents the grid of wells.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, grid_data: list[list[int]]):\n        self.wells = [Well(row) for row in grid_data]\n        self.num_rows = len(grid_data)\n        self.num_columns = len(grid_data[0]) if grid_data else 0\n\nclass Bucket:\n    \"\"\"Represents a bucket with a specific capacity.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, capacity: int):\n        self.capacity = capacity\n\n# --- Well Calculator (as per well_calculator.py) ---\nclass WellCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Contains core logic for calculating water and lowerings.\"\"\"\n    def calculate_total_water(self, grid_data: list[list[int]]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates total water units across all wells in the grid.\"\"\"\n        grid_obj = Grid(grid_data)\n        total_water = 0\n        for well in grid_obj.wells:\n            total_water += well.total_water_in_well\n        return total_water\n\n    def calculate_bucket_lowerings(self, total_water: int, capacity: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates bucket lowerings using total water and bucket capacity.\"\"\"\n        bucket_obj = Bucket(capacity)\n        return math.ceil(total_water / bucket_obj.capacity)\n\n# --- Main Entry Point Logic (condensed for max_fill function) ---\ndef max_fill(grid, capacity):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of times buckets need to be lowered to empty wells.\n    It sums water units and applies ceiling division for lowering operations.\n    \"\"\"\n    calculator = WellCalculator()\n    total_water = calculator.calculate_total_water(grid)\n    num_lowerings = calculator.calculate_bucket_lowerings(total_water, capacity)\n    return num_lowerings\n```"}
