{"task_id": "HumanEval/133", "solution": "```python\ndef sum_squares(lst):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of squares of ceiling-rounded numbers in a given list.\n    Each element is rounded up to the nearest integer before squaring.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _round_up(number: float) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Rounds a given float number up to the nearest integer.\n        This function handles both positive and negative numbers.\n        \"\"\"\n        # If the number is already an integer (e.g., 5.0, -2.0) or\n        # if the number is negative and has no fractional part greater than zero (e.g., -2.4 rounds to -2)\n        if number <= int(number):\n            return int(number)\n        # Otherwise, for positive numbers with fractional parts, round up.\n        else:\n            return int(number) + 1\n\n    def _square(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the square of a given integer.\"\"\"\n        return number * number\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for num in lst:\n        rounded_num = _round_up(num)\n        squared_num = _square(rounded_num)\n        total_sum += squared_num\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/132", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_valid_bracket_sequence(subsequence: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a string forms a valid, balanced bracket sequence.\"\"\"\n    stack = []\n    for char in subsequence:\n        if char == '[':\n            stack.append(char)\n        elif char == ']':\n            if not stack:\n                return False\n            stack.pop()\n    return not stack\n\ndef _has_nested_in_valid_sequence(valid_subsequence: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a valid bracket sequence contains at least one nested bracket.\"\"\"\n    # Nesting exists if the sequence is like [A] where A is a non-empty, valid bracket sequence.\n    if len(valid_subsequence) >= 2 and \\\n       valid_subsequence[0] == '[' and \\\n       valid_subsequence[-1] == ']':\n        inner_content = valid_subsequence[1:-1]\n        if inner_content and _is_valid_bracket_sequence(inner_content):\n            return True\n    return False\n\ndef is_nested(string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if there exists a valid subsequence (contiguous substring) with nested brackets.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(string)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            candidate_subsequence = string[i : j + 1]\n\n            if _is_valid_bracket_sequence(candidate_subsequence):\n                if _has_nested_in_valid_sequence(candidate_subsequence):\n                    return True\n    return False\n```"}
