{"task_id": "HumanEval/134", "solution": "```python\ndef check_if_last_char_is_a_letter(txt: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns True if the last character of a given string is an alphabetical character\n    and is not a part of a word, and False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(txt)\n\n    # FR3: Return False for empty strings.\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    last_char = txt[-1]\n\n    # FR4: Return False if the last character is not alphabetical.\n    if not last_char.isalpha():\n        return False\n\n    # At this point, we know n > 0 and last_char is alphabetical.\n\n    # FR5: Return True if txt has length 1.\n    if n == 1:\n        return True\n\n    # At this point, we know n > 1 and last_char is alphabetical.\n    second_last_char = txt[-2]\n\n    # FR6: Return True if the second-to-last character is not alphabetical.\n    if not second_last_char.isalpha():\n        return True\n\n    # FR7: Return False if the second-to-last character is also alphabetical.\n    return False\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/135", "solution": "```python\ndef can_arrange(arr):\n    \"\"\"Finds the largest index i where arr[i] < arr[i-1].\n    Returns -1 if no such index exists or for lists shorter than 2 elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) < 2:\n        return -1\n\n    # Iterate backwards from the second-to-last element down to index 1.\n    # The first 'i' found satisfying the condition will be the largest valid index.\n    for i in range(len(arr) - 1, 0, -1):\n        if arr[i] < arr[i-1]:\n            return i\n\n    # If the loop completes without returning, no such index was found.\n    return -1\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/136", "solution": "```python\ndef largest_smallest_integers(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest negative and smallest positive integers in a list.\n    Returns (None, None) if the list is empty or contains only zeros.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return (None, None)\n\n    negatives = []\n    positives = []\n\n    for x in lst:\n        if x < 0:\n            negatives.append(x)\n        elif x > 0:\n            positives.append(x)\n\n    largest_negative = None\n    if negatives:\n        largest_negative = max(negatives)\n\n    smallest_positive = None\n    if positives:\n        smallest_positive = min(positives)\n\n    return (largest_negative, smallest_positive)\n```"}
